<title>SOUTH KOREA: Samsung raises KorAm Bank stake.</title>
<headline>Samsung raises KorAm Bank stake.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Samsung Group's stake in KorAm Bank has recently risen to 17.6 percent from 14.25 percent, the Korea Stock Exchange said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The stake is owned by five of Samsung's units, including Samsung Electronics Co and Samsung Life Insurance Co, the exchange said in a statement.</p>
<p>Bank of America holds the biggest stake of 18.55 percent in KorAm Bank, while Daewoo Group holds a 11.81 percent stake through its member firms, a KorAm spokesman said.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5646</p>
</text>
